# BoschBite Insights 
BoschBite insights is a web-based dashboard for restaurants in the stellenbosch area, apart of the BoschCard loyalty programme. Vendors can sign in and see insights derived from BoschCard transactions data presented through feature such as the business dahsboard, leaderboard and calendar feature 

Our app was built using: 
* Refine: React framework with Material UI (MUI)
* Typescript 
* Vite: development server
* Supabase: database and authentication including Row Level Security sp each vendor only sees their own data 

The adaption document is included in ADAPTION.md which will explain how we adapted the requirements provided by the product owners 

## 1. Requirements 
Before you begin pelase ensure the following is installed on your computer:

| Requirement | Notes |
| ------------| ----- |
| Node.js | Download from nodejs.org. npm is installed automatically with Node.js|
| Git | Needed to cloe the repository |
| A web browser | E.g Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox. The app was mainly tested through Chrome and Edge |

To check that Node.js and npm are installed, please run: 
```
node -v 
npm -v
```
in your terminal.
Both commands should print a version number. If a version number is not returned these requirements may not yet be installed. 
> **Note :** you do not need to set up Supabase. The app connects to our existing Supabase project, and all tables, data and security rules are already in place

## 2. Installation 
### Step 1: close the Github repository from the Github bundle 
Open a terminal in the folder where the bundle file is saved and run:
```
git clone 6-honours-2026.bundle BoschBite-Insights-dev
cd BoschBite-Insights-dev
git checkout main
```
This creates a normal project folder called `BoschBite-Insights-dev` from the bundle and makes sure you are in the *main* branch 

### Step 2: Go into the app folder 
The app is installed inside the `BoschBite` folder, hence direct yourself into this folder using:
```
cd BoschBite
```
### Step 3: install the dependencies 
Once directed into the `BoschBite` folder, use:
```
npm install
```
This installs all the packages the app needs (including Refine and MUI). npm reads the `package.json` to see which packages the app requires, and `package-lock.json` to install the exact version needed.
> **Note :**  please use npm (over yarn) so that the versions in `package-lock.json` are used. 

## 3. Running the app
From inside the `BoschBite` folder, run: 
```
npm run dev
```
Then open the following address in your browser:
http://localhost:5173/ 
The app will open to the landing page, where you will be able to then sign in or sign up.
To stop the app, please select Ctrl + C in the terminal. 
> **Note :** Each time you want to run the app again, open the terminal, make sure to `cd` into the `BoschBite` file (if you are not already), and run npm run dev

## 4. Test accounts 
You can use the following test accounts to sign in. Each account has a different role, so the data and the functionality will change 
